to becoming a multifaceted entertainer.</i>

03:18.240 --> 03:21.300
So wait, you two met as child actors?

03:21.300 --> 03:25.370
Yeah, on set when we were little. 
We're basically childhood friends, right?

03:25.850 --> 03:27.440
Wrong!

03:27.440 --> 03:31.400
She was a seriously rude little gremlin, 
and even when we met again years later...

03:31.400 --> 03:33.100
The genius child actor who can 
lick baking soda just like that.

03:33.100 --> 03:35.610
The genius child actor 
who can cry in ten seconds flat!

03:35.900 --> 03:37.100
Cut that out!

03:37.100 --> 03:41.730
Lately, I've seen people wondering, 
"What's Baking Soda-chan's real name, again?"

03:42.390 --> 03:43.950
Sheesh.

03:45.640 --> 03:48.860
Okay, I think we got 
enough run time with that.

03:48.860 --> 03:50.390
Let's call it a day.

03:50.390 --> 03:51.750
Good work.

03:52.080 --> 03:55.370
You have a dance video shoot 
scheduled for tomorrow.

03:55.370 --> 03:57.880
The day after that, 
you have a Pieyon collab in the AM,

03:57.880 --> 04:00.610
and a collab livestream 
with pro gamers in the PM.

04:00.610 --> 04:03.780
And on the weekend, 
we have a concert in Hokkaido.

04:03.780 --> 04:05.470
Things sure have gotten busy.

04:05.760 --> 04:11.030
I'm beat, Miyako-san! 
Hug me and give me headpats!

04:09.590 --> 04:11.940
There, there. You're doing good.

04:12.350 --> 04:15.820
What now? Wanna go grab a bite?

04:15.820 --> 04:16.660
Nah.

04:16.660 --> 04:18.570
If we're done, I'm leaving.

04:19.880 --> 04:21.160
Me, too.

04:21.750 --> 04:23.120
Oh, okay.

04:23.540 --> 04:27.620
<i>Kana-chan and Ruby both seem 
to have changed a little.</i>

04:39.710 --> 04:42.590
I've decided to start dating Akane for real.

04:43.550 --> 04:44.650
So, you know...

04:48.030 --> 04:49.100
Get this.

04:49.100 --> 04:56.190
<b>Aqua-kun</b>

04:49.100 --> 04:53.440
The sound producer was yelling even more 
than the director. It was so scary.

04:53.440 --> 04:56.190
<i>Yeah, some people are old-fashioned like that.</i>

04:56.460 --> 04:59.060
<i>There's so much I want to vent to you.</i>

04:59.060 --> 05:00.400
When are you free next?

05:01.310 --> 05:06.420
If luck is with us, I'll be free the evenings 
of the 23rd and 29th this month.

05:06.420 --> 05:08.230
<i>Someone's gotten busy.</i>

05:08.230 --> 05:10.890
It's what happens when you have TV work.

05:11.330 --> 05:16.580
<b>Aqua-kun</b>

05:12.830 --> 05:14.210
Aqua-kun.

05:14.210 --> 05:15.030
<i>Hmm?</i>

05:15.030 --> 05:16.590
I wanna see you soon.

05:17.830 --> 05:19.960
Yeah. Me, too.

07:03.510 --> 07:06.270
<i>This is B-Komachi's second standalone concert!</i>

07:06.270 --> 07:08.740
<i>Thank you all for coming!</i>

07:10.640 --> 07:12.490
B-Komachi's second standalone!

07:12.490 --> 07:15.490
Just one year since formation, 
they sold out a 1K-capacity venue in minutes!

07:15.840 --> 07:18.210
<i>Streaming gang, are we here?</i>

07:15.990 --> 07:18.210
I'm so envious of those who got to go...

07:18.680 --> 07:21.200
I'm so glad they had paid streaming tickets!

07:21.200 --> 07:24.420
That's my MEMcho! 
She has a real nose for business!

07:21.950 --> 07:23.970
<i>We've got lots more to come!</i>

07:25.110 --> 07:27.920
<i>Next up is POP IN 2!</i>

07:25.110 --> 07:28.320
If you add up the live and streaming 
audiences, that's gotta be a lotta people!

07:28.320 --> 07:31.260
They could fill up arenas 
or even the Tokyo Dome, right?

07:31.260 --> 07:32.510
Don't be silly, you newb.

07:32.510 --> 07:42.020
<b>Exhibition Hall 7   Exhibition Hall 6   Exhibition Hall 5   Exhibition Hall 4   Exhibition Hall 3   Exhibition Hall 2   Exhibition Hall 1</b>

07:33.320 --> 07:38.660
Arenas? Even one block of Makuhari Messe 
has a minimum capacity of seven thousand.

07:38.660 --> 07:42.110
It's hard for even groups with 
a strong TV presence to fill them up.

07:42.410 --> 07:44.670
The Tokyo Dome is a whole different beast.

07:44.670 --> 07:48.190
The only idol groups that can 
perform there nowadays

07:46.320 --> 07:53.530
<b>Comuse</b>

07:47.150 --> 07:53.530
<b>Stardumst</b>

07:48.190 --> 07:52.890
are the ones backed by the biggest 
agencies. That's the era we live in.

07:53.480 --> 07:59.750
Not one underground female idol group 
has taken the stage there in the past 15 years.

08:00.900 --> 08:02.710
Keep your hopes in check.

08:02.710 --> 08:04.510
I don't know...

08:04.510 --> 08:05.210
Boss?

08:05.610 --> 08:09.560
Sure, showbiz has been 
dominated by major corpos lately.

08:10.030 --> 08:12.380
But since 2020,

08:12.380 --> 08:16.920
more and more musicians who got started on 
the Internet have had Tokyo Dome concerts.

08:17.330 --> 08:19.940
This could be a big turning point.

08:20.550 --> 08:25.890
From underground to Tokyo Dome? 
That's a rusty old dream of otaku everywhere.

08:25.890 --> 08:28.940
And it's quite likely that it'll be 
net idols who make it come true.

08:28.940 --> 08:32.120
You mean a group like B-Komachi?

08:32.120 --> 08:33.960
That's right.

08:33.960 --> 08:39.160
It'll take them at least four years to build 
a big enough fanbase for it, though.

08:39.580 --> 08:40.330
But...

08:40.870 --> 08:43.790
Not many can last that long.

08:44.710 --> 08:49.890
Kana-chan's a lot gloomier these days. 
She's not shining like the sun anymore.

08:49.890 --> 08:50.760
Really?

08:51.520 --> 08:53.830
I tend to notice these things about my faves.

08:54.370 --> 08:58.480
I've seen several idols make that face 
and quit the business shortly afterward.

08:58.480 --> 09:02.330
You could say the same about Ruby-chan, too.

09:02.330 --> 09:05.070
She used to be a lot more innocent and genuine,

09:05.440 --> 09:08.460
but now she feels cynical 
and calculated sometimes.

09:08.460 --> 09:11.000
<i>Never show me an old man 
calling her "Ruby-chan" again.</i>

09:11.490 --> 09:13.720
You think something happened?

09:14.600 --> 09:15.990
I can think of one thing...

09:15.990 --> 09:18.220
It can only be one thing.

09:20.330 --> 09:22.290
A new member joins!

09:22.540 --> 09:26.520
When girl groups get awkward, 
it's usually because of a new member.

09:26.520 --> 09:27.750
Yes, yes.

09:27.750 --> 09:31.340
In such times, good things might happen 
if you stick to stanning one single member.

09:31.340 --> 09:32.260
I see.

09:32.660 --> 09:34.280
TIL!

09:38.120 --> 09:39.820
Where's Aqu-tan today?

09:39.820 --> 09:42.660
It's filming day for <i>Dig Deep! 
Chase the Impawsible!</i>

09:42.660 --> 09:45.610
They shoot three episodes at a time, 
so they don't wrap until late.

09:46.440 --> 09:50.860
Miyako-san, drop me off at Ebisu. 
I have something to take care of.

09:51.830 --> 09:53.030
Oh, okay.

10:05.620 --> 10:07.150
What's up?

10:09.310 --> 10:10.360
MEM...

10:11.640 --> 10:15.500
What, you followed me here? 
Don't you live farther out?

10:15.960 --> 10:17.880
Kinda.

10:23.550 --> 10:28.360
I know you might not like me sticking 
my nose in your business like this...

10:29.580 --> 10:31.320
but it's about Aqu-tan, right?

10:31.770 --> 10:35.050
Anyone can tell you're having a rough time.

10:38.830 --> 10:41.500
It's been like this for the last six months.

10:42.150 --> 10:47.210
Whenever I visit the agency office, 
he retreats into his room.

10:48.030 --> 10:50.530
He didn't come to today's concert, either.

10:51.150 --> 10:51.920
Well...

10:51.920 --> 10:53.820
He's quite busy, too.

10:53.820 --> 10:56.430
No, he's avoiding me! I know it!

10:56.840 --> 11:01.430
He thinks he can't be around other girls 
because he's dating Akane Kurokawa now!

11:02.010 --> 11:04.480
What a show of loyalty.

11:04.480 --> 11:08.640
He's the most trustworthy boyfriend 
any girl could have.

11:09.900 --> 11:16.270
I know that Akane's talented, 
beautiful, and extremely nice.

11:16.270 --> 11:19.280
I'll gladly root for the two of them.

11:20.080 --> 11:23.630
And I'd never do anything to upset Aqua.

11:24.440 --> 11:26.900
So why does he have to avoid me 
like the plague?!

11:26.900 --> 11:29.960
It hurts me, you jerk!

11:29.000 --> 11:30.840
K-Kana-chan...

11:31.540 --> 11:33.460
There, there.

11:49.620 --> 11:52.650
Thanks for today. I'll be heading out.

11:52.650 --> 11:53.340
Good work.

11:53.340 --> 11:54.640
See you.

11:57.200 --> 11:57.950
Heya.

11:59.250 --> 12:00.280
MEM?

12:01.620 --> 12:05.250
I'm betting we didn't just happen 
to run into each other here,

12:06.300 --> 12:09.370
but I've been working since dawn and I'm tired.

12:09.370 --> 12:11.560
If you want to talk, save it for another—

12:11.560 --> 12:12.840
Another time?

12:12.840 --> 12:16.550
When will that be? Around a month from now?

12:17.230 --> 12:21.100
We both have packed schedules now.

12:21.100 --> 12:24.260
I wonder when we'll just happen 
to both be off on the same day.

12:26.230 --> 12:27.400
Fine.

12:27.820 --> 12:30.230
Let's at least take it someplace with a couch.

12:30.790 --> 12:33.690
Sure. In that case...

12:36.460 --> 12:40.530
FYI, adults aren't allowed to take 
unrelated minors around after 11 PM.

12:40.530 --> 12:41.880
It's banned by Tokyo ordinance.

12:41.880 --> 12:44.870
Guh! Let's not be a stickler for the rules!

12:49.010 --> 12:51.320
You seem worn out.

12:51.320 --> 12:53.540
We shot four episodes today.

12:54.750 --> 12:59.440
I've also got rehearsals 
and stuff for Lalalai's next play.

13:00.000 --> 13:02.500
I want to catch up on my studies 
once I get home, too.

13:02.500 --> 13:05.220
Oh, yeah. You're pretty smart, huh?

13:05.220 --> 13:06.560
Are you gonna go to college?

13:06.560 --> 13:07.560
That's the plan.

13:08.660 --> 13:11.090
It's the summer of my second 
year in high school.

13:11.090 --> 13:14.250
Anyone wanting to go to med school 
has to start hitting the books hard now.

13:14.250 --> 13:17.070
Med school? You wanna be a doctor?!

13:17.850 --> 13:19.160
I'm not sure...

13:20.820 --> 13:24.780
But thinking long-term, 
I want to keep that option open.

13:24.780 --> 13:27.310
Yeah, you should!

13:27.310 --> 13:32.570
I wish I could've gone to college, too! 
I'm proud of ya!

13:32.570 --> 13:36.250
It's not like you couldn't still do it.

13:36.250 --> 13:38.480
Just get a GED and take entrance exams.

13:39.670 --> 13:41.760
You're so naïve, Aqu-tan.

13:41.760 --> 13:45.340
Anyone who could think straight like that 
wouldn't be in showbiz to begin with!

13:45.340 --> 13:47.300
And that's no exaggeration!

13:47.300 --> 13:48.640
Uh, I'm pretty sure it is.

13:49.310 --> 13:54.640
Every adult in Japan knows that going to 
college improves your future prospects.

13:55.600 --> 13:59.820
But they don't do it, 
because they have their hands full.

14:00.570 --> 14:04.700
People don't always make 
the most rational decision.

14:05.230 --> 14:07.720
And that includes you, no?

14:08.400 --> 14:13.920
If you'd been more rational, you would've 
handled the Kana-chan thing better.

14:13.920 --> 14:15.630
I knew that's what this was about.

14:16.180 --> 14:18.870
You might want to stay out of it, though.

14:19.370 --> 14:24.090
I get that, but you know me. I don't always 
make the most rational decision, either.

14:24.790 --> 14:29.310
When I see a friend down in the dumps, 
I just wanna help them.

14:29.690 --> 14:31.380
That's just human.

14:31.770 --> 14:35.310
Kana-chan's performances 
have actually been getting worse!

14:35.310 --> 14:36.860
Do something about it!

14:36.860 --> 14:38.110
"Do something"?

14:38.850 --> 14:41.070
What more do you want me to do?

14:41.340 --> 14:43.400
I don't have an answer for you,

14:43.400 --> 14:47.030
but you can't just run away 
after pulling the moves on a girl.

14:47.030 --> 14:47.980
Excuse me?

14:48.530 --> 14:53.740
You're still so young that you probably 
don't know where to draw the line,

14:53.740 --> 14:58.130
but I'd say what you did to Kana-chan 
qualifies as leading her on.

14:58.740 --> 15:02.760
You should avoid that kinda thing 
unless you're really interested—

15:07.430 --> 15:12.820
You're one to talk after you brought a 
red-blooded boy home like it was nothing.

15:15.150 --> 15:16.350
Aqu-tan?

15:17.120 --> 15:20.990
I'm not exactly clueless when it 
comes to dating issues, you know.

15:21.520 --> 15:24.820
Quit talking down to me 
like you know it all, MEM.

15:25.290 --> 15:28.780
Once you decide to keep your distance, 
you can't half-ass it.

15:30.250 --> 15:37.250
Did you really think I wouldn't know 
that avoiding Arima would hurt her?

15:38.550 --> 15:42.590
Did you really think I <i>wanted</i> 
to do this to her?

15:43.410 --> 15:46.670
I've finally started to think 
about the future lately.

15:47.620 --> 15:50.550
Not just mine, but also those 
of the people around me.

15:51.160 --> 15:55.180
I have no doubt that Arima 
will become way more famous.

15:56.790 --> 15:59.150
Let me state the obvious here.

15:59.920 --> 16:03.840
When an idol is found to have a boyfriend, 
her fans don't take it well.

16:04.440 --> 16:06.430
What if the tabloids run an exposé?

16:06.430 --> 16:08.380
What if someone leaks it online?

16:08.780 --> 16:15.040
What if it gets out that Kana Arima has a 
lover, and a deranged fan takes it out on her?

16:16.350 --> 16:18.050
Whose fault would that be?

16:19.160 --> 16:22.920
What if he shows up 
at her place and murders her?

16:23.580 --> 16:24.990
Have you ever thought about that?

16:25.800 --> 16:29.740
I can't stand the thought 
of that happening again!

16:29.740 --> 16:32.800
<i>Maybe it's the other way around.</i>

16:33.450 --> 16:37.270
<i>Maybe I had it all wrong.</i>

16:37.780 --> 16:41.350
<i>I always thought Kana-chan 
was down bad for Aqu-tan.</i>

16:42.020 --> 16:43.640
<i>But maybe it's him.</i>

16:44.590 --> 16:48.430
<i>It's Aqu-tan who's got it bad for Kana-chan.</i>

16:56.210 --> 16:57.450
I get it now.

16:58.180 --> 16:59.580
I'm sorry.

17:03.620 --> 17:07.290
And this doesn't count as leading <i>me</i> on?

17:08.680 --> 17:11.360
I mean, people aren't always rational.

